ode6.irmos:
Cleanse me, O Savior,
for many are mine iniquities;
lead me up from the abyss of evils I pray Thee,
for unto Thee have I cried,
and Thou hast hearkened unto me,
O God of my salvation.

ode7.irmos:
Once in Babylon the fire stood in awe
of God's condescension;
for which sake the youths in the furnace,
dancing with joyous steps as in a meadow, chanted:
O God of our fathers, Blessed art Thou!

ode8.irmos:
In his wrath the Chaldean Tyrant made the furnace blaze,
with heat fanned sevenfold for the servants of God;
but when he perceived that they had been saved by a greater power
he cried aloud to the Creator and Redeemer;
'ye children bless, ye priests praise,
ye people, supremely exalt Him throughout all ages'.

ode9.katavasia:
From fear it may be easier,
for us to prefer silence,
for though not fraught with danger, O Virgin,
it is difficult to fashion hymns fittingly wrought for thee.
Yet, O Mother, grant us the power to chant in such a way,
insofar as it is our will.
